# `GXScaffold.BTZ.Uniformization` — uniformization of GH Cauchy-compact Cauchy-maximal `𝔼₀`-manifolds

Packages WP-41n, WP-43f, WP-44g, WP-46h, WP-47g. `papers/gx` §4.6 (`RamcovGX.tex:2348–2396`);
rulings DEC-28, DEC-31/119, DEC-75/76/77, DEC-106, DEC-107/117, DEC-118, DEC-119, DEC-126.
**0 `sorry`; every declaration on standard axioms** (`campaign/WP-47g/axioms.out`; the upstream
mixed-diamond leaf is proved in `GXScaffold.BTZ.AbsMax`, WP-47f, and the developed BTZ half-line
in `GXScaffold.BTZ.FutureRay`, WP-47e).

* **`prop:globally_hyperbolic_cauchy_complete_manifolds`** — `RamcovGX.tex:2348`, CLOSED in its
  corrected form (DEC-77, DEC-27), marked. Form of record `GX.btz_isBTZFutureComplete_C1`: GH +
  Cauchy-maximal + a compact `C¹` spacelike Cauchy surface (DEC-107) + a BTZ point (`s ≥ 1`) +
  `π₁(Reg M)` not metabelian (implied by DEC-119's free and non-abelian) ⇒ for every developing
  pair and presentation, the chartwise `M̃` extending `𝒟` exists and EVERY such `M̃` is future
  complete in DEC-118 (a)'s reading, `BTZTildeData.IsBTZFutureComplete` (both inclusions of
  `J⁺` and `I⁺` at every point, BTZ points included; the developed BTZ line by
  `GX.futureRay_null_supset`). The printed statement is refuted with its printed hypothesis
  (DEC-31 = `GX.IsE0CauchyComplete`) and its ruled conclusion: `GX.e0PastHalf_counterexample_DEC118`.
* `theo:globally_hyperbolic_cauchy_complete_cauchy_maximal` — `RamcovGX.tex:2363`, partial by
  DEC-28 ALONE (the Cauchy-compact strengthening, which DEC-28 rules partial under DEC-27); EVERY
  assertion of the DEC-28 form proved, `defi:BTZtop` on `𝒟(M̃)` and « isomorphism » of singular
  manifolds included (WP-47g fixer, rounds 1–2), no reading left open. Form of record
  `GX.btz_uniformization`: for `M` GH, Cauchy-maximal, with a compact `C¹` spacelike Cauchy surface,
  a BTZ point, `π₁(Reg M)` free and non-abelian (DEC-76/119), and every developing pair `(𝒟, ρ)`:
  a loxodromic (DEC-75); `ρ` faithful, discrete, torsion-free; the `ρ(Γ)`-invariant null planes
  `Π_w`; `𝒟(Reg M̃) = Ω⁺ = ⋂ I⁺(Π_w)` (future case PROVED, DEC-77 (a)); `Reg M ≅ ρ(Γ)\Ω⁺`; and on
  ONE chartwise `M̃` with tamifying `T_BTZ` (DEC-106/118/119): `𝒟` **injective on all of `M̃`**,
  `M̃` GH (natural topology), future complete and future distinguishing, `𝒟 ∘ φ = ρ(φ)·𝒟` for every
  deck `φ`; the **rays** `Δₓ = 𝒟(sing M̃) ∩ J⁺(𝒟x) ∖ {𝒟x}` (`GX.btzTildeDelta`, `x` BTZ) are
  relatively open future complete lightlike rays `{𝒟x + λu, λ > 0}`, in `∂Ω⁺`, a `ρ(Γ)`-invariant
  family, with `⋃ Δₓ = 𝒟(sing M̃)` disjoint from `Ω⁺` and **`𝒟(M̃) = (⋃ Δₓ) ∪ ⋂ I⁺(Π_w)`**
  (DEC-28's display); and **`ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃) ≃ₜ M`**, `[𝒟 e] ↦ p(e)`, `𝒟(M̃)` with **`defi:BTZtop`
  near the rays** (`GX.btzRangeTop`: `𝐌³`'s topology and the sets `I⁺(p) ∪ ]p,+∞[`, `p ∈ ⋃ Δₓ`),
  PROVED equal to the `𝒟`-image of `T_BTZ` (`GX.BTZTildeData.btzRangeTop_eq_devImageTop`,
  l.2390–2395), the homeomorphism agreeing on `Ω⁺` with `Reg M ≅ ρ(Γ)\Ω⁺`; and it is an
  **isomorphism of singular `(Isom 𝐌³, 𝐌³)`-manifolds** (l.2374, l.2397; the twins'
  a.e.-isomorphism reading, `GX.btz_quotient_chart`, `GX.tamely_singular_manifold_admits_aeIso`):
  `ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃)` carries the UNIQUE maximal a.e. atlas making the projection `M̃ → ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃)`,
  `e ↦ [𝒟e]`, an a.e. morphism (`M̃` with `p^*B_M`, `prop:singular_manifold_branched_covering`),
  and for it `h` and `h⁻¹` are a.e. morphisms (`GX.btzTilde_quotient_aeIso`).

Proved here, of general use (0 `sorry`, standard axioms only):

* `GX.uniformization_range_eq_of_absMax`, `GX.uniformization_of_absMax`: Barbot's equality
