  charts), `GX.hasDerivAt_chartMap_slice` (the sector chart along `τ = −1` is a local isometry
  of `|dz|²`), `GX.norm_sub_le_integral_norm_deriv_complex`,
  `GX.ofReal_norm_sub_le_lintegral_of_lipschitzOnWith`, `GX.ofReal_norm_sub_le_of_zeroFree`
  (an FTC inequality across the zero set of a curve).

> \begin{prop} Globally hyperbolic Cauchy-complete $\BTZ$-manifolds are future complete.
> \end{prop} \begin{proof} From Theorem 3 of \cite{brunswic2021cauchy} the regular par of $M$ is
> globally hyperbolic and Cauchy-complete. Barbot uniformization Theorem \cite{barbot_globally_2004}
> then implies future completeness of the regular part. Finally Lemma 2.4 of
> \cite{brunswic2021cauchy} implies that the singular locus contains full future BTZ rays.
> \end{proof} (l.2348–2353)

> \begin{thm} Let $M$ be a globally hyperbolic Cauchy-complete Cauchy-maximal $\mass{0}$-manifold,
> let $\widetilde M$ its maximal covering branched over $\sing(M)$, of developing map and holonomy
> $(\D,\rho)$. […] Then, up to time reversal of $M$: $\D$ is injective; $\rho$ is faithful,
> discrete and torsion-free; there exists a $\Gamma$-invariant family of relatively open future
> complete lightlike rays $(\Delta_i)_{i\in I}$ and a $\Gamma$-invariant family of lightlike planes
> $(\Pi_j)_{j\in J}$ such that $\D(\widetilde M) = \bigcap_{i\in I} J^+(\Delta_i) \cup
> \bigcap_{j\in I} I^+(\Pi_j)$; endowing $\D(\widetilde M)$ with the BTZ topology in the
> neighborhood of the lightlike rays $(\Delta_i)_{i\in I}$, the developing map induces an
> isomorphism $M\xrightarrow{~~\overline \D~~} \rho\backslash\D(\widetilde M)$. \end{thm}
> (l.2363–2376)

## Hypothesis checklist (forms of record `btz_uniformization`, `btz_isBTZFutureComplete_C1`)

| paper / ruling | here |
|---|---|
| `M` globally hyperbolic (l.2363) | ✓ carried: `(CE M).GloballyHyperbolic` (ETT's, the charted causality of `M`; it is the bridge structure's, `E0Bridge.globallyHyperbolic_e0ManifoldCausality_iff`) |
| Cauchy-complete (l.2363) | ⚠ strengthened (DEC-28): Cauchy-compact, read per DEC-107 as `∃ S, E0Surgery.IsE0C1SpacelikeCauchy M S` (B21 l.227; no smoothing, DEC-117) |
| Cauchy-maximal (l.2363) | ✓ carried: `IsE0CauchyMaximal M` (DEC-77 (c)) |
| finite type, `π₁(Σ∖sing)` non-abelian, `s ≥ 1` (DEC-76) | ✓ read (DEC-119): `π₁(Reg M)` free (`IsFreeGroup`) and non-abelian; `s ≥ 1` ✓ `(chartedSing e0SingY M 0).Nonempty`. (The prop's form takes « not metabelian », which free non-abelian implies) |
| "up to time reversal" (dropped, DEC-77 (a)) | ✓ the future case is concluded and PROVED |
| `M` second countable | ⚠ carried (implicit in « manifold »; Cor 2.18's form) |
| the given pair `(𝒟, ρ)` (l.2365) | ✓ every developing pair of `Reg M` is a hypothesis |
| `M̃` and `𝒟` on it (DEC-106/119) | ✓ through the bridge: every presentation `Φ` of `\widetilde{𝔼₀}`, ONE chartwise `\widetilde M`-datum `d` with tamifying `T_BTZ`, `d.D = 𝒟` on `reg M̃`, injective, GH in the natural topology |
| `𝒟` injective | ✓ on `Reg M̃` and on ALL of `M̃` (`btz_injective_dev_C1`, in the form of record) |
| `ρ` faithful, discrete, torsion-free | ✓ |
| `D(M̃) = (⋃Δᵢ) ∪ ⋂ I⁺(Πⱼ)` (DEC-28's display) | ✓ `range d.D = (⋃ₓ Δₓ) ∪ Ω⁺`, `Ω⁺ = ⋂ I⁺(Π_w)`; each `Δₓ` relatively open, future complete, lightlike, in `∂Ω⁺`; the family `ρ(Γ)`-invariant (the family is existential in the statement; the witness is indexed by the BTZ points, SCOPE (b) (iii)) |
| `M ≅ ρ\D(M̃)`, BTZ topology near the rays (l.2373; DEC-106: `T_BTZ` here only) | ✓ `𝒟(M̃)` with `defi:BTZtop` near the rays, `btzRangeTop` (generated by `𝐌³` and `I⁺(p) ∪ ]p,+∞[`, `p ∈ ⋃ Δₓ`), PROVED `= devImageTop` (`btzRangeTop_eq_devImageTop`, the proof's l.2390–2395); homeomorphism `ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃) ≃ₜ M` (`btzTilde_quotient_homeomorph_btzTop`), agreeing on the regular classes with the isometry `Reg M ≅ ρ(Γ)\Ω⁺` (`btzTilde_quotient_compat`); ✓ « isomorphism » of singular manifolds (SCOPE (b) (ii)): `h`, `h⁻¹` a.e. morphisms for the unique maximal a.e. atlas on `ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃)` making `M̃ → ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃)` an a.e. morphism (`btzTilde_quotient_aeIso`) |
| prop: « future complete » (`def:manifold_future_complete_all` over `M̃`) | ✓ DEC-118 (a)'s ruled reading `BTZTildeData.IsBTZFutureComplete M d` for every chartwise `d` extending `𝒟`, both inclusions at every point (the developed BTZ line: `futureRay_null_supset`, WP-47e) |
| prop's counterexample, printed hypothesis Cauchy-complete (DEC-31/119) | ✓ `IsE0CauchyComplete {τ<0}` PROVED; `¬ IsBTZFutureComplete` for EVERY datum of `{τ<0}` PROVED |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* (a) **The future-case selection** (DEC-77 (a)) is PROVED: in the past case
  `𝒟(Reg M̃) = Ω⁻(Λ)` is past complete, which `GX.false_of_sing_of_pastComplete` refutes.
* (b) **The BTZ half (WP-47g), and the one reading the headline row rests on.** Built:
  `btz_uniformization_btzRays` (§4h) — equivariance at the BTZ points (`btzTilde_dev_deck`:
