  proof's l.2390–2395, through the basic neighbourhoods of `J⁺(Δ₀)`
  (`btzJ0_exists_basic_of_mem_nhds`), a chart sending `Δ₀` onto the developed half-line with its
  orientation (`btzTilde_chart_align`), and the regular points of a BTZ chart being off `Δ₀`
  (`BTZTildeData.exists_nhds_sing_of_mem_btzLine`); the homeomorphism is stated for
  `btzRangeTop` (`btzTilde_quotient_homeomorph_btzTop`). (ii) **PROVED (WP-47g fixer round 2)**: « isomorphism » (l.2374, l.2397 « isomorphism of
  singular E-manifolds ») in the a.e.-isomorphism sense the library certifies for the twins
  `prop:quotient_chart` (`GX.btz_quotient_chart`) and `rem:tamely_singular_manifold_admits`
  (`GX.tamely_singular_manifold_admits_aeIso`): `M` with `E0Bridge.e0SingularGXStructure`
  (DEC-119), `M̃` (natural topology, DEC-106) with `p^*B_M` (maximal,
  `singular_manifold_branched_covering`), `ρ(Γ)\𝒟(M̃)` with the quotient topology of
  `btzRangeTop` and the maximal a.e. atlas `h^*B_M`, the UNIQUE maximal one making
  `e ↦ [𝒟 e]` an a.e. morphism (the quotient structure of `prop:aeGXquotient`'s form); `h` and
  `h⁻¹` are a.e. morphisms (`btzTilde_quotient_aeIso`, through `btz_aeIso_of_homeomorph_comp`),
  and on the regular classes `h = f⁻¹ ∘ π` for the isometry `Reg M ≅ ρ(Γ)\Ω⁺`
  (`btzTilde_quotient_compat`). (The previous round's sentence « `ρ\𝒟(M̃)` carries no singular
  `(G,X)`-structure in the library » was wrong — `SingularGXStructure`, `IsAEMorphismOf`,
  `existsUnique_aeGXQuotient` are there — and is withdrawn.) (iii) not a reading: the
  family `(Δᵢ)` of l.2368 is existential; its witness here is indexed by the BTZ points `x` of `M̃`
